<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  AppWidgetProviderInfo for the first widget this app ships.

  Sizing — 4x2 cells (250dp x 110dp minimum), which fits the four-row layout
  and the header/footer. The rows share the leftover height evenly, so a
  two-deadline account does not leave a hole in the middle of the card.
  `targetCell*` is the Android 12+ hint; `min*` is the fallback the older
  launcher maths uses.

  Preview — `drawable-nodpi/widget_preview.png`, cropped from a screenshot of
  the widget running on a device. A `previewLayout` would render the static
  layout XML without the renderer having run, i.e. an empty card in the picker,
  so the PNG is the only way to show real content.

  The previous PNG was hand-drawn and had drifted: it showed two rows above a
  hole and English copy ("12 days left", "as of 09:41") in an app whose default
  language is Vietnamese. It was a picture of the very layout bug that was then
  fixed. Regenerate it from a fresh screenshot whenever the row layout changes —
  a preview that lies about the widget is worse than no preview.

  Update period — SIX HOURS. Android floors periodic widget updates at 30
  minutes and batches them; a widget update is not a free background job. The
  app pushes an immediate repaint whenever it captures a new snapshot (foreground
  or a deadline-changing write), so the periodic tick only exists to roll the
  day-count over and let the "as of" footer age. Four local repaints a day is
  enough for a value that changes at midnight, and `onUpdate` does no network
  I/O — only a preferences read plus RemoteViews construction. See
  `WarrlyDeadlineWidgetProvider` for the full rationale.

  Category — `home_screen` only, never `keyguard`: a deadline list with the
  user's device names is not lock-screen content. See the privacy note next to
  the receiver in AndroidManifest.xml.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:description="@string/widget_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/warrly_deadline_widget"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/widget_preview"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="21600000"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    tools:targetApi="31" />
